\nGiven the constraints — one bet only, long only, $10–$20 notional — the downside of betting is small ($10–$20), but the instruction framework rewards correctness against rules, and there's no stated reward for betting vs. skipping. As a trader with no edge, the disciplined choice is to skip when there's no favorable setup. The \"Intern\" persona presumably should be conservative.\n\nAlternatively, one could argue: in a game where you must eventually allocate, betting on SHIB (the relative outperformer, least negative) long is the \"strongest\" of a weak bunch. But \"least bad\" isn't \"good.\" Momentum logic says avoid longs in a downtrend; mean-reversion logic says buy the dip. Without resolution, no bet = no expected loss.\n\nI'll skip. The JSON skip form:\n\n{\"v\":1,\"round\":1993899,\"nonce\":\"e22af1b9b5a12bd2\",\"action\":\"skip\"}\n\nThat matches the template exactly with the given round (1993899) and nonce (\"e22af1b9b5a12bd2\"). One line, nothing else.\n\nWait — should I reconsider betting on PEPE for an oversold bounce? Let me weigh: PEPE -11.10% in 24h. Deep single-day drops in memecoins frequently continue into the next session, especially when the whole sector is red — sector-wide weakness suggests it's a beta move, not idiosyncratic flush-and-revert. Longing anything into sector-wide distribution is coin-flippy at best. With no funding/discount data to give an edge, skip is correct.\n\nAlso note the round number and nonce must match exactly. Round: 1993899. Nonce: e22af1b9b5a12bd2. Yes.\n\nFinal answer: the skip JSON line."},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null,"matched_stop":154827}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","created":1794509101,"usage":{"prompt_tokens":451,"total_tokens":1311,"completion_tokens":860,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"reasoning_tokens":828,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":828}}}